Sval: a cancelled font load logs no error

gfxUserFontEntry::FontDataDownloadComplete logs every unsuccessful
download as a console error, NS_BINDING_ABORTED included. A document that
navigates away or closes while a font of its own is loading cancels that
load with NS_BINDING_ABORTED, so a fast click from a page logged a font
failure that never happened. A cancelled load logs nothing.

diff --git a/gfx/thebes/gfxUserFontSet.cpp b/gfx/thebes/gfxUserFontSet.cpp
index c3ff1a8e54..3c489771f5 100644
--- a/gfx/thebes/gfxUserFontSet.cpp
+++ b/gfx/thebes/gfxUserFontSet.cpp
@@ -873,7 +873,9 @@ void gfxUserFontEntry::FontDataDownloadComplete(
       fontSet->LogMessage(this, aSrcIndex,
                           "font-display timeout, webfont not used",
                           nsIScriptError::infoFlag, aDownloadStatus);
-    } else {
+    } else if (aDownloadStatus != NS_BINDING_ABORTED) {
+      // A load the document cancelled, as when it navigates away, has not
+      // failed.
       fontSet->LogMessage(this, aSrcIndex, "download failed",
                           nsIScriptError::errorFlag, aDownloadStatus);
     }
